      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142713",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/b5/b5b4d260ad31b6c4efc3f7314e98df8b422f8d92f0f21fa436334c4b15d88a67.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n = 80$ from a large population where some individuals have a particular characteristic. Given that the proportion of those in the sample with the characteristic is $p^(^) = 0.7$, find a $90%$ confidence interval for the population proportion $p$ of individuals having this characteristic.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.645) = 0.05$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
