      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142715",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a sample of size $n = 100$ from a large population where some individuals have a particular characteristic. Given that $65%$ of the sample has the characteristic, find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population proportion of individuals having this characteristic.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.96) = 0.025$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
